{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa's Part-Time Job", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "From Nine to Five", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Achievement Test > Achievement Test", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Showing Interest", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You show interest in people you meet by asking them common personal questions, often related to their work.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">You can ask colleagues casual questions about:</span> <br /><li>their commute to work<br /><li>what part of the city they live in <br /><li>what they like for lunch<br /><li>their family life", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">You avoid asking colleagues personal questions about: </span> <li>their romantic life<br /><li>personal health conditions<br /><li>detailed family history", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How long does it take you to come to work?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When did you start working here?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How do you like your job?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"content": "engenn4le18ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "almost there", "type": "name"}, {"content": " almost finished a task or almost arrived at a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: <span class=\"strong\">Boss</span>: Did you complete that expense report? <br/><span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: I'm almost there. Just a few more pages.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le18ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about work.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "portions", "type": "name"}, {"content": "certain amounts of food to serve one person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The sauce portions for each cheesecake must all taste the same.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le18ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "saucepan ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a round cooking pan  used for frying or making sauces ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The saucepan must be heated up before the cooking starts.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le18ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to catch on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become better at a new process of work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa is really catching on with the daily routine at her chef job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le18ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to show me the ropes ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show a new person at work how something is done  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Daniel is showing Vanessa the ropes, so she's learning quickly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le18ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "culinary ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " related to cooking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa gained a lot of culinary skills from college.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le18ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to demonstrate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to show with action how something is done ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa demonstrates fine culinary skills in her cooking.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le18ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Talking About Obligations (What you have to do)", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When describing our job responsibilities, we use <span class=\"italic\">have to  + infinitive </span> to talk about an obligation or things that are necessary to do.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " I have to put strawberries on the cake. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have to work every day. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Choose your current job or imagine a job that you want to have in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 5 sentences describing what you have to do in this job. e.g., <span class=\"italic\">I have to work weekends.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read one sentence to your partner. He/she will try to guess what job you are describing. If they can't guess, read another one.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you are finished, listen to your partner and try to guess the job he/she is describing. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write sentences about a job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about what I have to do in my job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to my partner's job description and try to guess the job.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le18ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn4le18ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn4le18ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "1", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: Vanessa, did you chop the vegetables?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Almost there.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: After that we need to prepare all the daily sauce portions."}, {"image": "engenn4le18ob10re2img05.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "9000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I already have the saucepans all set. First, I have to place the strawberries on the cheesecake slices.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span> : You're catching on to the routine."}, {"image": "engenn4le18ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "19000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Thanks. I have you showing me the ropes.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: So, how did you like the culinary course at college? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I learned a lot. I was in the kitchen every day for 4 hours, so I felt like I was already working."}, {"image": "engenn4le18ob10re2img05.jpg", "id": 4, "time": "34000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: Well, you certainly demonstrate that you have the skills.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Thanks. When did you start as a chef?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: Oh, I started cooking about 20 years ago.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Amazing. That's why you're so good at so many recipes. I hope you can teach me more.<br />"}], "coverimg": "engenn4le18ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": "<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: Vanessa, did you chop the vegetables?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Almost there.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: After that we need to prepare all the daily sauce portions.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I already have the saucepans all set. First, I have to place the strawberries on the cheesecake slices.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span> : You're catching on to the routine.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Thanks. I have you showing me the ropes.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: So, how did you like the culinary course at college? <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I learned a lot. I was in the kitchen every day for 4 hours, so I felt like I was already working.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: Well, you certainly demonstrate that you have the skills.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Thanks. When did you start as a chef?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Daniel</span>: Oh, I started cooking about 20 years ago.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Amazing. That's why you're so good at so many recipes. I hope you can teach me more.<br />", "type": "p"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "text", "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I ca